From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:24:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 166/342] Remote Control: profiles for the ODROID remote and
 the JVC RM-RK52

The add-on writes them when the user has no profiles yet:
- Hardkernel's ODROID remote (NEC, address 0xb2; codes from Linux's
  rc-odroid keymap and Hardkernel's LIRC file): arrows, OK, back, home,
  menu, and the system volume and mute;
- the JVC RM-RK52, a car stereo remote (JVC, address 0x8f, learned on
  the board): MediaPlayer's play/pause, mute, full screen, next and
  previous file, wind and volume.

The preferences always give BInputDevice::Control() a message: it adds
it to the request and empties it for the reply, and crashed on NULL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devices/remote_control/Jamfile            |   1 +
 .../devices/remote_control/Presets.cpp        | 114 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../devices/remote_control/Presets.h          |  23 ++++
 .../remote_control/RemoteControlDevice.cpp    |   8 +-
 .../remotecontrol/RemoteWindow.cpp            |   6 +-
 5 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/add-ons/input_server/devices/remote_control/Presets.cpp
 create mode 100644 src/add-ons/input_server/devices/remote_control/Presets.h

diff --git a/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/remote_control/Jamfile b/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/remote_control/Jamfile
